ssociative classification categorization of MEDLINE articles into MeSH keywords</article-title><source>IEEE Eng Med Biol Mag</source><year>2007</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17441608</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1109/MEMB.2007.335581</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sohn</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Comeau</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilbur</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimal Training Sets for bayesian prediction of MeSH assignment</article-title><source>J Am Med Inform Assoc</source><year>2008</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>546</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18436913</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1197/jamia.M2431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mark&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Daumke</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hahn</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cross-language MeSH indexing using morpho-semantic normalization</article-title><source>AMIA Annu Symp Proc</source><year>2003</year><fpage>425</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14728208</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soualmia</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>&#x000c9;tude et &#x000e9;valuation d'approches multiples de projection de requ&#x000ea;tes pour une recherche d'information intelligente. Application au domaine de la Sant&#x000e9; sur l'Internet</article-title><source>PhD thesis</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>INSA de Rouen, France</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Claveau</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000e9;billot</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Fabre</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bouillon</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Learning Semantic Lexicons from a Part-of-Speech and Semantically Tagged Corpus using Inductive Logic Programming</article-title><source>Journal of Machine Learning Research (JMLR), special issue on ILP</source><year>2003</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>493</fpage><lpage>525</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1162/153244304773936036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ozdowska</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Claveau</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inf&#x000e9;rence de r&#x000e8;gles de propagation syntaxique pour l'alignement de mots</article-title><source>TAL (Traitement Automatique des Langues)</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>186</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cussens</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>D&#x0017e;eroski</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><collab>(Eds)</collab></person-group><source>Learning Language in Logic</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Lecture Notes in Artificial Intelligence, Springer Verlag</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.springer.com/computer/artificial/book/978-3-540-41145-1"/></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muggleton</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Raedt</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inductive Logic Programming: Theory and Methods</article-title><source>Journal of Logic Programming</source><year>1994</year><volume>19/20</volume><fpage>629</fpage><lpage>679</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.36.8300"/><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0743-1066(94)90035-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Srinivasan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>The ALEPH manual</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Machine Learning at the Computing Laboratory, Oxford University</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Agrawal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Imielinski</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Swami</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mining Association Rules Between Sets of Items in Large Databases</article-title><source>Proceedings of the SIGMOD Conference, Washington, DC, USA</source><year>1993</year><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>216</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plotkin</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Meltzer B, Michie D</surname></name></person-group><article-title>A Note on Inductive Generalization</article-title><source>Machine Intelligence</source><year>1970</year><volume>5</volume><publisher-name>Edinburgh: Edinburgh University Press</publisher-name><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>163</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation cit